{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>כי</b> (for), <b>מצוה</b> (commands) — decrees, as in: כי הוא צוה ונבראו (for He commanded and they were created)." "<b>רסיסים</b> — from the context, these are smaller fragments than בקיעים (cracks). R. Moses the Kohen said: רסיסי לילה (drops of the night) is fine rain. Know that rain, which is a body, and likewise air, which is wind, is a body, only it is very fine. Some say: the meaning is 'the great house' — the prince and his men."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:21.797104412Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}